,"rank":110,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":10283565597655,"type":"album","name":"La historia de El Rey","artist":"José Alfredo Jiménez","year":2005,"weight":4,"yt":"ZipzeNiBe_E","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":327,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":1761350111138,"type":"album","name":"The Best of Carlos Gardel","artist":"Carlos Gardel","year":1998,"weight":4,"yt":"2JbC42_t2TY","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":591,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":188966023995861,"type":"album","name":"Yuyay Jap'ina Tapes","artist":"Luzmila Carpio","year":2014,"weight":3,"yt":"Y8joPFS-oS0","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":704,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":138140975025832,"type":"album","name":"Del Danzón al Cha cha cha","artist":"Various Artists","year":2000,"weight":3,"yt":"zZQh4IL7unM","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":146,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":126452639057954,"type":"album","name":"Na balada","artist":"Michel Teló","year":2012,"weight":3,"yt":"iCXwU6nEQYo","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":416,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":118772389839796,"type":"album","name":"El folklore de Chile, vol. VIII: Toda Violeta Parra","artist":"Violeta Parra","year":1961,"weight":3,"yt":"XaYC0GRCLyE","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":165,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":39471147823988,"type":"album","name":"Garifuna Music: Field Recordings from Belize","artist":"Various Artists","year":2005,"weight":3,"yt":"SzA94_1JIPg","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","rank":225,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Boom in the United States","body":"Tiny Desk has been credited by many media outlets as one of the major forces behind the boom of Latin music in the United States. The platform's commitment to showcasing Latin artists has led to some of its biggest successes. \"Hasta el punto de que muchos medios consideran al Ténidé, como uno de los grandes responsables del bom de la música latina en Estados Unidos.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"De Tiny Desk a Boiler Room: El Boom de los Conciertos en YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QPTMemJ4ZUA"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Breakout Success (2010s)","body":"Latin music experienced a significant breakout in the 2010s, with artists like Bad Bunny achieving widespread success globally. This period marked a substantial increase in its international reach and popularity. \"Latin music busted out all over.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 5: Music and Tech","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mNqqLDpUuZY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Increased Appreciation via Live Platforms","body":"Paradoxically, thanks to these direct music platforms, many people who previously had reservations about Latin music are starting to appreciate it. The intimate and unfiltered nature of these performances allows new audiences to connect with the genre. \"Mucha gente que antes tenía recelo hacia la música urbana, por latina, están empezando a apreciarla.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"De Tiny Desk a Boiler Room: El Boom de los Conciertos en YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QPTMemJ4ZUA"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Influence on Joe Jackson","body":"Joe Jackson absorbed Latin sounds and met mambo and salsa in Latin clubs during his time in New York City in the early 1980s, particularly when Hector LaVoe was dominant. These influences significantly informed his songwriting and recording for his \"Night and Day\" album. \"In Latin clubs, Jackson heard salsa and met Engay at a time when Hector LaVoe was dominant. This, too, informed his songwriting and recording.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Angry Young Men Edition Part 2","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"International Explosion via YouTube","body":"Latin music experienced an international explosion in popularity due to YouTube. The platform's global reach and monetization capabilities eliminated geographic barriers, allowing music to exist in a \"borderless world.\" \"Latin music exploded.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Rise and Fall and Future of the Music Video - Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7IDbqdIw3WU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Joe Jackson's Deeper Infusion","body":"Joe Jackson's 1984 album \"Body and Soul,\" recorded in New York City, was infused with an even greater influence from Latin pop and jazz. This reflected his ongoing exploration and integration of the diverse musical cultures he encountered in the city. \"infused with even greater influence from Latin pop and jazz.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Angry Young Men Edition Part 2","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Use of Mutes","body":"Mutes are employed in Latin music to alter the volume or tonal quality of brass instruments, helping them blend with other ensemble members. \"They're used in Latin music.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Explainer 4","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D8GU8ZpSgY8"}]}]}